{
  "_comment": "Canonical cross-runtime plinko:v1 test vectors. Reproducible by any runtime (native Rust, wasm, TS) from the pinned algorithm below. All values are integer/ppm; no floating point. Generated by an independent python3 reference: libs/games/scripts/gen_vectors.py.",
  "algorithm": {
    "game_type": "plinko:v1",
    "seed_derivation": "seed = blake2b-256 of b'game-seed|'+game_type+'|'+server_seed+'|'+client_seed+'|'+action_index.to_le_bytes(i32) with action_index=0 (the place-bet). The outcome is sealed at bet time; the later cashout (index 1) is a settle trigger only and derives nothing",
    "path": "path[i] = bit (i % 8) of seed byte (i / 8), for i in 0..rows (0 = left, 1 = right); rows <= 16 so only the first 2 seed bytes are consumed",
    "bin_index": "number of 1-bits in path (popcount) \u2014 Galton board",
    "multiplier": "multipliers_ppm[bin_index] from the (rows, risk) table below; tables are frozen constants compiled into the kernel, symmetric (m[k] == m[rows-k]); the house edge is baked into the values",
    "payout": "stake * multiplier_ppm / 1e6 rounded half-up (exact for integer stakes: at most 6 decimal places). Paid on cashout or on the settles_at deadline-sweep \u2014 identically, because the settle action cannot change the sealed outcome",
    "config_borsh": "place-bet action payload = borsh(Config { rows: u32 LE, risk: enum u8 (0=low, 1=medium, 2=high) })",
    "rtp": "exact per-table RTP under the binomial bin distribution P(bin=k) = C(rows,k) / 2^rows: rtp_ppm = rtp_weighted_sum / rtp_denominator = sum(C(rows,k) * multipliers_ppm[k]) / 2^rows. Every table lands in [995000, 995500] ppm",
    "supported_rows": [
      8,
      10,
      12,
      14,
      16
    ],
    "supported_risks": [
      "low",
      "medium",
      "high"
    ],
    "scale_ppm": 1000000,
    "rounding": "half-up (midpoint away from zero), mirroring game-engine-core/src/fixed_point.rs"
  },
